{"name":"Colorado Dawn","hex":"#e09cab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"colorado","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cigar of medium color and strength.","A fish of the species Lutjanus colorado, the Colorado snapper."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/colorado"},{"term":"dawn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To begin to brighten with daylight.","To start to appear or become obvious."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The morning twilight period immediately before sunrise.","The rising of the sun."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dawn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Colorado","blocks":[{"text":"Colorado is a landlocked state in the Mountain West subregion of the Western United States. It is part of the Southwestern United States, sharing the Four Corners region with Arizona, New Mexico, and Utah. It is also bordered by Wyoming to the north, Nebraska to the northeast, Kansas to the east, and Oklahoma to the southeast. Colorado is noted for its landscape of mountains, forests, high plains, mesas, canyons, plateaus, rivers, and desert lands. It encompasses most of the Southern Rocky Mountains, as well as the northeastern portion of the Colorado Plateau and the western edge of the Great Plains. Colorado is the eighth-largest U.S. state by area and the 20th by population. The United States Census Bureau estimated the population of Colorado to be 5,957,493 as of July 1, 2024, a 3.2% increase from the 2020 United States census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Flag_of_Colorado.svg/330px-Flag_of_Colorado.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colorado"},{"title":"Dawn","blocks":[{"text":"Dawn is the time that marks the beginning of twilight before sunrise. It is recognized by the appearance of indirect daylight being scattered in Earth's atmosphere, when the centre of the Sun's disc has reached 18° below the observer's horizon. This morning twilight period will last until sunrise, when direct daylight outshines the diffused light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Desert_Dawn.jpg/330px-Desert_Dawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mexican_Cession_in_Mexican_View.PNG/500px-Mexican_Cession_in_Mexican_View.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Mexican_Cession_in_Mexican_View.PNG/500px-Mexican_Cession_in_Mexican_View.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Map of the Mexican Cession, with the white representing the territory the United States received from Mexico (plus land ceded to the Republic of Texas) after the Mexican–American War. Well over half of Colorado was received from this treaty.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMexican_Cession_in_Mexican_View.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Chiving1.jpg/250px-Chiving1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/71/Chiving1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Chiving1.jpg/250px-Chiving1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"John Chivington, commander of the 3rd Colorado Cavalry at the Sand Creek Massacre.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChiving1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/John_Evans_with_daughter_Josephine%2C_c._1859.png/500px-John_Evans_with_daughter_Josephine%2C_c._1859.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par